WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.837
Nominal variables distinguish categories without placing them in a meaningful order.

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:09.107
Blood types are different, but one blood type is not greater than another.

00:00:09.107 --> 00:00:14.892
ZIP codes and patient IDs are common traps because they may contain digits.

00:00:14.892 --> 00:00:21.592
Counts and proportions are natural summaries, and bar charts are usually a good starting visualization.

00:00:21.592 --> 00:00:26.182
The important rule is not to invent numerical meaning for a label.

00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:32.507
The easiest way to classify a variable is to ask what statements are meaningful in the real world.

00:00:32.507 --> 00:00:40.577
Can values only be different, can they be ordered, are differences meaningful, and does zero mean absence?

00:00:40.577 --> 00:00:46.572
Those questions are more reliable than looking at whether the software stores the column as an integer or

00:00:46.572 --> 00:00:48.055
floating-point number.
